# snapshots/ is ALLOW-BY-DEFAULT. It used to be `snapshots/*` plus a growing list
# of negations, which meant every NEW file added there vanished silently — three
# snapshot regression tests each needed their own `!` line, and the third
# (authorizeSnapshotTierPolicy.test.js) was written, looked committed, and would
# have run zero files forever until someone noticed. Nobody thinks to check
# .gitignore after adding a test. Deny-by-default in a source directory hides
# work; deny the specific things instead.
#
# p1authz-export.snapshot.json used to be excepted here because it carried live
# `clientSecret`/`password`/`token` values. A redacted copy was tracked for a
# while, then deleted outright: it was an ad-hoc export of a DIFFERENT PingOne
# environment (legacy financial policies, not the AI Demo tree), nothing
# referenced it, and it kept getting mistaken for the live-tree export that
# snapshots/merge-mcp-amount-bands.js needs as input. snapshots/ still has no
# ignore exceptions.
# ⚠️ If you export from PingOne, the raw file WILL contain live secrets.
# Redact `clientSecret`, `password`, and `authenticationAttributes.token` before
# committing — this repo has already had live PingOne credentials in its history
# once. Better: keep exports outside the repo entirely.
certs/
.codegraph/
# graphify knowledge graph — local index only; regenerated by `graphify update .`
graphify-out/
# ...but knowledge bundles in graphify-out/ ARE version-controlled (authored knowledge)
!graphify-out/*.kb.json
# Git worktrees (isolated development workspaces)
.worktrees/
worktrees/
# Staged source for Code Explorer image COPY (regenerated by build-codegraph.py
# --stage-src on setup/run). Docker dev bind-mounts the live repo instead.
langchain_agent/repo-src/
demo_api_server/bin/pingcli

# --- Secret/backup hygiene (stop stale-data + secret leaks) ---
# Local env files with real secrets (never commit; use *.example templates)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# `npm run setup:fresh` / `pingone:bootstrap` output. Rewritten on every run and
# carries worker client secrets and demo passwords — its own header says "Do not
# commit it", but it was tracked from #370 until 2026-08-03, so anyone who ran
# either script silently staged live credentials.
setup-config.md
# Scratch file for hand-keeping the current demo username/password while working.
# Untracked and unignored, it showed in `git status` at the repo root — one
# `git add -A` from the same public-history leak that forced the 2026-08-29
# rotation. It also backs off sync-main-checkout.sh, whose DIRTY_OUTSIDE_NOISE
# check exempts only untracked `.claude/*.md`, so the launchd sync would stall
# silently. Credentials are better kept outside the repo entirely.
users.txt
# App-generated config/import backups (were committed by accident)
*.bak
demo_api_server/.env.pre-import-*
demo_api_server/data/backups/
demo_api_server/data/runtimeData.json.bak
# Agent-gateway-config editor rotating backups (written next to the edited
# file, e.g. /.backups for scope-topology.json via the compose /repo mount)
.backups/
# Env backups with a suffix after .bak (e.g. .env.bak-3006) that *.bak misses
.env.bak*
**/.env.bak*
# dotenvx private decryption key (vault→dotenvx cutover). Holds DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY,
# which decrypts every encrypted `.env` — same sensitivity as VAULT_PASSWORD was.
# NEVER commit; delivered at runtime via env only (run.sh/run-docker.sh read it).
# The encrypted `.env` files themselves stay ignored by the `**/.env` rules above.
.env.keys
**/.env.keys

# --- Runtime/generated artifacts (churn on every run — never track) ---
# Playwright test output
demo_api_ui/test-results/
# Root-level test-run reports (generated markdown; root-anchored so it only
# matches ./test-results, not any nested demo_api_* dirs)
/test-results/
# Server activity log
demo_api_server/logs/
# Runtime data store — rewritten on every mutation and holds captured request
# state (Authorization headers etc.). Seed data lives in the tracked
# bootstrapData.json; store.js falls back to it when runtimeData.json is absent.
demo_api_server/data/runtimeData.json
# LMDB runtime store — lock file AND the DB itself.
# The DB was previously tracked as seed data. It is not needed for that:
# bankingDb.js seeds from data/store.js whenever the store is empty
# (`if (!hasData) _seed()`), so a fresh clone builds its own.
# Tracking it was actively harmful — the running BFF bind-mounts and writes
# this file, so it showed as permanently dirty, and every sync-main-checkout
# run stashed it, reverting live demo state and stranding it in a stash.
demo_api_server/data/persistent/lmdb/lock.mdb
demo_api_server/data/persistent/lmdb/data.mdb
# Per-machine MCP client config — holds machine-specific paths and must never
# hold credentials. Copy .air/mcp.json.example to .air/mcp.json to set up.
.air/mcp.json
# Per-machine Cursor MCP config — tenant-specific OAuth client id; copy from
# .cursor/mcp.json.example or let install.sh patch from demo_api_server/.env.
.cursor/mcp.json
# Personal Claude Code allowlist/settings — never committed (hygiene check 3).
.claude/settings.local.json
# Written by scripts/sync-main-checkout.sh on every run; read by npm run sync:status.
.claude/sync-status.json
# A .claude note kept aside because it diverged from the tracked copy (see
# reconcile_parked_docs in scripts/sync-main-checkout.sh).
.claude/*.md.local
# SE DevOps kubeconfig backup (credentials — never commit; use install-se-kubeconfig.sh)
.local/kube/*
!.local/kube/README.md

# evidence screenshots/results from the real e2e evidence + use-case suites (never commit)
/demo_api_ui/evidence/

# Loose LLM/provider API-key scratch files kept in the repo root (never commit).
# Real keys belong in the gitignored service .env files; these are the ad-hoc
# notes people paste them into first.
/claude-switch-keys.txt
*-keys.txt
*.key


# pac.jar is a 33MB Ping-supplied binary — set PAC_JAR instead of committing it.
/pac/pac.jar

# Ad-hoc scratch files that accumulate in the repo root. Left untracked they
# trip scripts/sync-main-checkout.sh's "unexpected dirty files" guard, which
# then refuses to fast-forward — so the Docker stack (which bind-mounts the
# main checkout) silently keeps serving pre-merge code after every PR.
/amountAsCode.yaml
/restrictions.yaml
/content-api.zip
/out.txt
/README (1).md
/agentless-mcpgw/
/agentless-mcpgw-*.tgz
/privgateway-*.tgz
/pingone-privgateway-helm-main.zip
/deploy-privgateway.prompt.md
/privilege/agentless-mcpgw-values.*.yaml

# Encrypted credential vault — NEVER commit. This repo is PUBLIC, and the vault's
# AES-256-GCM ciphertext is only as strong as VAULT_PASSWORD, which is the same
# string as the demo account password. 441eb756 (#1104) removed that literal from
# the working tree, but it is still reachable in history, as are two secrets.vault
# blobs — see docs/incident-response/vault-history-exposure.md. Committing the vault
# publishes every credential inside it. Keep the file local: vaultLoader treats a
# missing vault as a clean no-op ('no_vault_file') and falls back to .env /
# process.env, and run-docker.sh handles its absence explicitly.
/secrets.vault
/secrets.vault.audit.log
# In-flight envelopes from vault save()/createVault. Complete ciphertext, same
# sensitivity as the vault itself; a crash between write and rename leaves one
# behind. The glob covers both the legacy `.tmp` name and the per-writer
# `secrets.vault.<pid>.<rand>.tmp` form.
/secrets.vault*.tmp

# Privilege proxy enrollment token (contains tenant secrets)
ping-mcpgw/config/proxy-token

# Privilege gateway OIDC env — written at runtime by the Settings modal (PUT /env)
# into this bind-mounted repo dir; contains OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET. Never commit it.
ping-mcpgw/config/pingone.env

# Regenerated per environment by snapshots/merge-mcp-amount-bands.js — a merge of
# a LIVE policy export, so machine-specific and large. The merger is source;
# its output is not.
snapshots/mcp-amount-bands.merged.snapshot.json
